title: The 'good person' lie
description: A post from the channel: Satan promotes the false idea that all it takes to be righteous is to be a "good person."
output: lessons/posts/post-good-person-lie-and-self-righteousness.html

# From the post of 2022-01-13 (studies/data/notes/post-good-person-lie-and-self-righteousness.html), in the author's words.
# The post cites "1 Thessalonians 2:11-12"; the verses quoted are 2 Thessalonians 2:11-12.

=== The lie
--- The 'good person' lie [title]
overline: A post from the channel
heading: The 'good person' lie
sub: Fooling even the best of us into adopting wickedness as good.
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

--- Most people
p: Most people conflate preference for principle.
p: Most people wish-cast reality away for the thing that lets them behave the way they want, now.
p: Most people put their lusts and desires in the same mental space as needs.
p: Very few will advocate for the right thing if it doesn't directly favor them.

--- Just be a "good person"
lead: This tendency to rationalize and project is why Satan promotes the false idea that all it takes to be righteous is to be a "good person." To try to be "moral."
p: They can manipulate and shift the window on what makes one moral, fooling even the best of us into adopting wickedness as good.

--- What damns so many
lead: This false belief in our own works, and ability to be self-righteous, is what damns so many to hell.
p: It's why the majority are so susceptible to manipulation.

=== The scripture
--- None righteous
scripture: Romans 3:10; Romans 3:23

--- Strong delusion
scripture: 2 Thessalonians 2:11-12

--- The free gift [title]
heading: The free gift
take: It's why it's so hard for those with the humility to accept the free gift of salvation to be deceived by a lie.
read: app:doctrine-salvation | Salvation by grace through faith
